{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clustering analysis clustering analysis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md","fileName":"Clustering Analysis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clustering Analysis","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 22:42\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Distributed Data Mining and Clustering]] · [[Cluster Analysis Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Distributed Data Mining and Clustering","Cluster Analysis Foundations","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clustering analysis clustering analysis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md","fileName":"Clustering Analysis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clustering Analysis","heading":"Clustering Analysis","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Clustering analysis divides observations into groups so members of the same group are more similar to one another than to members of other groups. It is unsupervised because no supplied class label defines the desired partition.\n\nResults depend on the similarity measure, representation, algorithm, parameters, and assumed cluster shape; a partition is not meaningful independently of those choices.\n\nThe introductory treatment in *Cluster Analysis and Data Mining* frames clustering as a sequence of explicit choices: select attributes, define proximity, form groups whose within-group similarities exceed between-group similarities, choose a stopping level, and validate the interpretation. A clustering is therefore conditional on its representation, objective, parameters, and intended use.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Distributed Data Mining and Clustering","Cluster Analysis Foundations","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clustering analysis clustering analysis","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clustering Analysis.md","fileName":"Clustering Analysis.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clustering Analysis","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf]]\n\n[[clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Distributed Data Mining and Clustering","Cluster Analysis Foundations","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}